      "headline": "Pixels2Actions",
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "This week, Google DeepMind shows a world model you can steer in real time.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/v_g1_5s.png",
            "overlay": "A world you can steer",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Researchers test whether a frontier AI model can really run a robot, and where it fails.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "split",
            "items": [
              {
                "src": "assets/v_s5_12s.png",
                "label": "Frontier model on real robots",
                "cue": "frontier"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/v_z3_4s.png",
                "label": "Trained only in simulation",
                "cue": "run"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "SenseNova et al. · ZAP project page (Luma AI)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Plus a startup whose robots learn from one demonstration, Toyota building robotaxis for Waymo, and self-driving excavators.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "panels",
            "items": [
              {
                "src": "assets/v_m0_18s.png",
                "label": "One demo",
                "cue": "robot"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/t_car.png",
                "label": "Toyota × Waymo",
                "cue": "toyota"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/b_photo.png",
                "label": "Excavators",
                "cue": "excavators"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Machenta · Toyota · Bedrock Robotics via TechCrunch"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Five stories, in plain English.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Five stories. Plain English.",
            "sub": "October 25 – November 1, 2026"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "Genie 4: a world you can steer",
      "source": "deepmind.google",
      "sourceDate": "Oct 27, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://deepmind.google/blog/genie-4-a-new-generation-of-world-simulation/"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story one. Google DeepMind announced Genie 4, its new world model.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_hero.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "A world model is an AI that generates a world as you move through it.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "⌨️",
                "label": "You act",
                "sub": "keys or a text prompt",
                "cue": "you"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🧠",
                "label": "Model generates",
                "sub": "the next moment",
                "cue": "generates"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🌐",
                "label": "World responds",
                "sub": "in real time",
                "cue": "move"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Think of a video game with no game engine. The AI itself draws what happens next.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/g_clip_world.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "In DeepMind's recordings, people steer with keyboard controls, and use text prompts to change the scene as it evolves.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/g_clip_steer.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It's also DeepMind's first real-time world model to generate audio natively.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/v_g9_4s.png",
            "pan": "out",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "So why is this on a robotics channel?",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Why robots care"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "DeepMind says Genie 4 can help with developing training environments for robots and agents.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_robots.png"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Like a flight simulator, but for robots: a safe place to practice, in endless variations.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "✈️",
              "title": "Flight simulator",
              "sub": "Pilots practice before the real thing",
              "cue": "flight"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "🤖",
              "title": "World model",
              "sub": "Robots could practice in generated worlds",
              "cue": "robots"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "On the announcement page, a simulated robot arm holds a pipette and dispenses liquid into a lab plate.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/g_clip_pipette.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "And DeepMind's Gemini 4 Argon works with Genie 4 to simulate Apptronik's Apollo humanoid playing checkers,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/g_apollo_sim.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "breaking the task down into real-time steps.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "split",
            "items": [
              {
                "src": "assets/g_apollo_steps.png",
                "label": "Gemini 4 Argon: steps",
                "cue": "breaking"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/g_apollo_sim.png",
                "label": "Genie 4: simulation",
                "cue": "steps"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. DeepMind pitches world models as safe training grounds for robots, and it's already experimenting with Genie 4 alongside its Gemini Robotics work.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "🌐",
                "label": "Generated world",
                "sub": "Genie 4",
                "cue": "world"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🤖",
                "label": "Robot training ground",
                "sub": "the pitch",
                "cue": "training"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🦾",
                "label": "Gemini Robotics",
                "sub": "experiments",
                "cue": "experimenting"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. Those robot clips are generated simulations. DeepMind doesn't say any robot was trained in Genie 4, and it gives no benchmark numbers.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Real-time, steerable, with native audio",
                "cue": "reality"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Robot clips are generated simulations",
                "cue": "generated"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "No robot reported trained in it",
                "cue": "trained"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "No benchmark numbers",
                "cue": "benchmark"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "reality"
        },
        {
          "narration": "DeepMind also says details and object permanence can still drift over time.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_drift.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "For now, it's a research preview for trusted testers.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_preview.png",
            "stamp": "Preview"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "PAPER",
      "headline": "Can GPT-6 Astra run a real robot?",
      "source": "SenseNova et al. · arXiv",
      "sourceDate": "Oct 15–30, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://www.sensenova.ai/has-gpt-6-astra-achieved-embodied-intelligence",
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22471",
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.41320",
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35817"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story two. Frontier AI models, like one called GPT-6 Astra, can now directly control robots.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/s_hero.png",
            "credit": "Source: sensenova.ai"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "But how well?",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "But how well?"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Here's the setup. The model sees camera images, works out a plan, and sends motion commands through a harness, a software layer that works like an interpreter for the robot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "📷",
                "label": "Sees",
                "sub": "camera images",
                "cue": "sees"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🧠",
                "label": "Plans",
                "sub": "the frontier model",
                "cue": "plan"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🔌",
                "label": "Harness",
                "sub": "turns plans into motion calls",
                "cue": "harness"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🦾",
                "label": "Robot moves",
                "cue": "commands"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "First, a big report led by SenseNova, published earlier in October.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/s_absdate.png",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.22471 · Oct 15, 2026"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "In simulation, GPT-6 Astra scored ninety-nine to one hundred percent on six benchmark suites,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/s_sim_c.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "badge": "99–100% in simulation",
            "badgeCue": "ninety",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.22471 (SenseNova et al.)"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "but with help: it was allowed to learn in context from the benchmark's training set.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/s_10x.png",
            "credit": "Source: sensenova.ai"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "On real robots, simple pick-and-place worked: seventeen of eighteen trials.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/s_clip_pnp.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "But plug insertion, which needs precise contact, went zero for eleven, across three robot platforms.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "from": 0,
                "to": 0,
                "suffix": "/11",
                "label": "real plug insertions",
                "cue": "zero"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.22471 (SenseNova et al.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "In the report's own findings, cloth folding and long mobile tasks were also markedly harder.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/s_plug_c.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.22471 (SenseNova et al.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The authors' verdict: competent, but not yet practical.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Competent, not yet practical",
            "sub": "SenseNova et al.: “not yet that of practical embodied intelligence”",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.22471 (SenseNova et al.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Two new preprints this week try to close that gap.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Two fixes",
            "sub": "LEXP · ZAP"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The first, LEXP, gives the model a notebook of lessons. After each attempt, it extracts lessons and reuses them later, without retraining the model.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "🦾",
                "label": "Try",
                "sub": "a real task",
                "cue": "attempt"
              },
              {
                "icon": "📝",
                "label": "Extract lessons",
                "sub": "what happened",
                "cue": "extracts"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🔁",
                "label": "Reuse",
                "sub": "on the next actions",
                "cue": "reuses"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Across twelve real-world tasks, success rose from five point six percent for plain Astra, to sixty-three point nine percent.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "from": 5,
                "to": 5,
                "suffix": ".6%",
                "label": "plain Astra",
                "cue": "five"
              },
              {
                "from": 63,
                "to": 63,
                "suffix": ".9%",
                "label": "with LEXP",
                "cue": "sixty"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.41320 (LEXP)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Those are the paper's own trials, on a two-armed robot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/l_639_c.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.41320 (LEXP)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The second, ZAP from Luma AI, teaches a small open model its motion skills entirely in simulation,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/z_clip_sim.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "with no real-world robot data.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/z_abs.png",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.35817 (ZAP, CC BY 4.0)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "On a real two-armed robot, it succeeded on twenty-nine of thirty trials,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/z_clip_real.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "matching GPT-6 Astra in the same harness.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/z_2930.png",
            "credit": "Source: arXiv:2610.35817 (ZAP, CC BY 4.0)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. The ZAP authors put it this way: their model already understands robot tasks, and mainly lacks motion control.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "🧠",
              "title": "Understanding",
              "sub": "Already there, per ZAP",
              "cue": "understands"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "✋",
              "title": "Motion control",
              "sub": "The missing skill",
              "cue": "lacks"
            }
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. These are preprints with small trial counts, and precise contact, like plugging something in, was the weak spot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Real-robot trials, with counts",
                "cue": "reality"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Preprints, small trial counts",
                "cue": "preprints"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "Plug insertion: 0/11",
                "cue": "precise"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "reality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "Robots that learn from one demo",
      "source": "machenta.com · x.com/Ed__Johns",
      "sourceDate": "Oct 27, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://machenta.com/blog/instant-robot-learning",
        "https://x.com/Ed__Johns/status/2115030792720031996"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story three. A startup called Machenta came out of stealth, saying its robots learn a new task from a single demonstration.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_blog.png",
            "credit": "Source: machenta.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Founder Ed Johns announced a forty million dollar seed round, co-led by Creandum and USV.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/m_tweet_c.png",
            "fit": "contain",
            "credit": "Source: x.com/Ed__Johns · Oct 27, 2026"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Here's the usual way to teach a robot: collect hours or days of demonstrations, then train for hours or days.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "⏳",
              "title": "The usual way",
              "sub": "Hours or days of demos, then hours or days of training",
              "cue": "usual"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "👆",
              "title": "Machenta's claim",
              "sub": "Show it once. No training, no waiting.",
              "cue": "train"
            }
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Machenta's pitch is like showing a new coworker a task once.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Show it once"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "In its videos, a person demonstrates once, on objects the robot has never seen,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/m_clip_demo.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "then rearranges them and steps back, and the robot does the task on its own.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/m_clip_auto.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The company says the model was trained entirely in simulation, without a single pixel of real-world training data.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_sim.png",
            "credit": "Source: machenta.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The idea is to use simulation to learn how to learn, not to memorize one task.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "📼",
              "title": "Memorize",
              "sub": "one task at a time",
              "cue": "memorize"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "🧩",
              "title": "Learn to learn",
              "sub": "pick up new tasks from one demo",
              "cue": "learn"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Machenta says the same model runs on six different robots.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_six.png",
            "credit": "Source: machenta.com"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Here, several of them work a line together, in a one-person factory demo.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/m_clip_factory.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "To stress-test it, Machenta ran self-resetting tasks for an hour each:",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_stress.png",
            "credit": "Source: machenta.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "seventy-four of seventy-four block placements, seventy-eight of seventy-eight screwdriver handovers, and ninety-seven of ninety-nine attempts at standing a bottle upright.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "from": 0,
                "to": 74,
                "suffix": "/74",
                "label": "block placements",
                "cue": "seventy-four"
              },
              {
                "from": 0,
                "to": 78,
                "suffix": "/78",
                "label": "screwdriver handovers",
                "cue": "seventy-eight"
              },
              {
                "from": 0,
                "to": 97,
                "suffix": "/99",
                "label": "bottle stand-ups",
                "cue": "ninety"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Source: machenta.com (self-reported)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. Machenta claims one demonstration is enough to learn a new task.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/v_m0_25s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Machenta"
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "If that holds up, teaching a robot becomes as quick as showing it once.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "👆",
                "label": "Show once",
                "cue": "teaching"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🤖",
                "label": "Robot does it",
                "cue": "quick"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. Machenta itself calls these tasks relatively simple.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_simple.png",
            "stamp": "Self-reported",
            "credit": "Source: machenta.com"
          },
          "section": "reality"
        },
        {
          "narration": "The blog mentions no paper or code, and there's no independent evaluation yet.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Uncut demo videos, six robots",
                "cue": "blog"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Company's own numbers, simple tasks",
                "cue": "mentions"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "No paper or code mentioned",
                "cue": "paper"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "No independent evaluation yet",
                "cue": "independent"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "Toyota will build robotaxis for Waymo",
      "source": "global.toyota",
      "sourceDate": "Oct 30, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://global.toyota/en/newsroom/corporate/44960881.html"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story four. Toyota and Waymo announced the next phase of their self-driving partnership.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/t_none.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Toyota will build an autonomous version of its bZ4X for Waymo's ride-hailing service.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "clip",
            "src": "assets/t_clip_car.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The whole build happens under one roof, at Toyota's Takaoka plant in Japan, from assembling the base vehicle to integrating Waymo's self-driving hardware.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "🏭",
                "label": "Base vehicle",
                "sub": "assembled by Toyota",
                "cue": "assembling"
              },
              {
                "icon": "📡",
                "label": "Waymo hardware",
                "sub": "integrated on site",
                "cue": "integrating"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🚕",
                "label": "Robotaxi",
                "sub": "bZ4X for Waymo",
                "cue": "hardware"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Think of a phone that leaves the factory with its key apps already installed.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Built in, at the factory"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "That's straight from Toyota's release.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/t_takaoka.png"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
